es gave investors a snapshot of contrasting fortunes in the sector.\nFireEye (NASDAQ:FEYE) jumped about 11% following its bullish earnings report after the bell yesterday.\nThe cybersecurity company beat expectations on the top and bottom lines. It also guided profit and revenue in line with analyst expectations.\nFireEye has had a volatile year of trading, but is ramping up close to around the $19 level, heights not seen since April.\nOn the flip side, Electronic Arts (NASDAQ:EA) fell about 3%, continuing a miserable trend for the stock that began in July.\nSince that time, when the company warned about a delay in the latest incarnation of its popular Battlefield game series, the stock has tumbled around 40% (falling from near $150 to about $90 today).\nThe videogame maker beat expectations for the most recent quarter after the bell yesterday but warned on revenue for the current quarter and on profit for fiscal 2019.\nRelated Articles\nCisco Rises 3%\nRussia stocks higher at close of trade; MOEX Russia up 2.29%\nItaly stocks higher at close of trade; Investing.com Italy 40 up 0.24%", "external_links": ["https://www.investing.com/news/technology-news/fireeye-earnings-boosted-by-lower-costs-higher-subscriptions-1666660?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=yahoo_finance&quot;", "https://www.investing.com/equities/fireeye-inc-earnings?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=yahoo_finance&quot;", "https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/cisco-rises-3-1668282?utm_source=yahoo&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=yahoo_finance&quot;", "https://www.investing.com/news/technology-news/fireeye-earnings-boosted-by-lower-costs-higher-subscriptions-1666660?utm_source=yahoo&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=yahoo_finance", "https://www.investing.com/equities/fireeye-inc-earnings?utm_source=yahoo&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=yahoo_finance", "https://s.yimg.com/ny/api/res/1.2/f.FSG8_tZlR_g6S.lAmt3Q--~A/YXBwaWQ9aGlnaGxhbmRlcjtz